<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sinhalese–Portuguese War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1527">1527</a>–<a href="/years/1658">1658</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sinhalese–Portuguese War was a long series of conflicts in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> between the Portuguese and the Sinhalese kingdoms of Sitawaka and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kandy">Kandy</a>. Portugal gained control of most of the coastal lowlands, but its invasions of the highland kingdom of Kandy were destroyed at Danture in 1594 and Randeniwela in 1630. Kandy allied with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>, who drove the Portuguese from the island by 1658.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sinhalese-portuguese-war.jpg" alt="Sinhalese–Portuguese War" width="320" height="251" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johannes Janssonius Waasbergen (publisher), Anoniem / Anonymous (engraver / etcher) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AMH-6978-KB_The_Portuguese_Pedro_Lopez_welcomes_the_Empress_of_Ceylon,_Dona_Catharina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
